## Research summary

I couldn't reach the network in this environment (WebFetch/WebSearch/curl were all denied), so I grounded the decision in this repo's own prior art plus my training knowledge of Spring Data Couchbase:

- **No existing precedent needs Docker for Couchbase.** `metadata/com.couchbase.client` and `tests/src/com.couchbase.client` only cover `metrics-micrometer` and `tracing-micrometer-observation` — never the core `java-client`. There is no Couchbase image pinned under `tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/resources/allowed-docker-images/`.
- **Strong direct precedent exists for the wrapping module.** `tests/src/org.springframework.boot/spring-boot-data-couchbase/4.1.1` (already merged, commit `0377c66108`) tests `DataCouchbaseAutoConfiguration` purely via `ApplicationContextRunner` — property binding, `CouchbaseMappingContext`, `MappingCouchbaseConverter`, `CouchbaseCustomConversions`, `TranslationService` — with **no live cluster, no Docker, no extra dependencies** beyond the default scaffold (library + assertj-core). It notably never asserts on `CouchbaseTemplate`, the one bean that needs a real connection — evidence the author deliberately stayed inside the no-infra boundary.
- `org.springframework.data:spring-data-couchbase` is the raw module behind that autoconfiguration, so the same boundary (mapping/conversion/annotation processing without a live `Cluster`) is reachable here too.
- The one gap: if generation goes further and exercises repository-proxy creation / derived-query building (`CouchbaseRepositoryFactory`, `PartTree`-based queries) — valuable because dynamic proxies are exactly what native-image reachability metadata cares about — it needs a test double for `CouchbaseOperations`, since there's no real cluster available. This repo already has precedent for exactly this shape of problem (`kafka-streams` adds `mockito-core` as `testImplementation` to mock a collaborator it can't bring up for real).

★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────
The preflight record is parsed by `library_preparation_preflight.py`: `agent_guidance` only reaches the downstream generation prompt when `action` is `advisory_preparation` — for `no_action` it's silently dropped. That's why steering advice (even without a hard dependency) belongs under `advisory_preparation`, not folded into a `no_action` summary.
─────────────────────────────────────────────────

